Z||000000||varnster||09-16-2001||06:29 PM||||new cal, rotors, pads, disconected master cyl,(painted the booster) hooked it all back up, and started bleeding front driver side with my mity vac all is good, then go to pass side, no brake fluid coming out of bleeder, go to all remaining wheels and again no fluid. And the master cylinder level is not droping I pumped the brake no help, and worked the vac pump for about 20 min with not a drop coming out, left bleader open for the last hour nothing! whats wrong? ||||reg||8
Z||000001||varnster||09-16-2001||08:18 PM||||I feel a little silly, I pumped the shiooly<BR>out of the brake peddel and it finnaly came <BR>out! but I dont think im using this damn vacume pump correctly, is the hose from the<BR>bleader tit to the resovoir fill up with brake fluid at some point! or what! this is<BR>the first time I have done this and the handbook doesnt help for sh--! can someone<BR>speak shadytree to me!||||reg||9
Z||000002||Indiana_resto_guy||09-16-2001||09:15 PM||||Sounds like your using the pump the way its supposed to be hooked up. The bleeder needs to be opened just a small amount or it will suck air. Is there a gauge on it?<BR>By the way, the correct way to bleed brakes is to start at the farthest from the master cylinder.<BR>Sometimes it takes a while to fill the calipers with fluid. I fill them first, seems to go faster.<BR>Are you certain that there is no air in the master cylinder?||||reg||1
Z||000003||varnster||09-16-2001||09:46 PM||||There probly is some air in the master cylinder, but I just painted under the hood <BR>and didnt want to spill any brake fluid on the paint when I disconect to bench bleed. I thought using a vacume pump it would suck it<BR>into a vac and purge any air.Im just not getting a good stream of fluid coming out the bleaders,it just kinda spurts how long should it take to get a good solid stream?<BR>Thanks for the help resto!||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||09-16-2001||11:57 PM||||try wrapping the bleeders with a little teflon tape. screw them in but not all the way closed. then vac bleed.<P>vac bleeder might get the air from the MC but don't count on it. read my brake service article and the extra bit about MC bleeding linked off it.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif"> <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
